{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/388811-the-existence-of-the-multiverse-and-the-meaning-of-choice","id":388811,"title":"The existence of the Multiverse and the meaning of choice.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-02-01T13:23:40-08:00","id":388811,"title":"The existence of the Multiverse and the meaning of choice.","content":"<span style=\"color:#141823\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">There is a pressing question that I have had for some time. Imagine for one moment that there are an infinite number of realities out there, a multiverse, each one created by the different choices we have made and the ones we haven't. My question is, does the existence of other realities formed by our alternative choices make the very act of choice meaningless? I mean, what is the point of making any choice if out there in the infinity there is a universe in which we made the opposite choice? What meaning has any of our choices with infinite universe? I'm curious to know your opinions. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=1tag9Pm3qtA\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=1tag9Pm3qtA\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=1tag9Pm3qtA\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=1tag9Pm3qtA </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2964,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","user":"Firanai","date":". 02-01-2015, 05:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-01T13:50:00-08:00","id":388844,"title":"","content":"Why did you post this when someone else might have in another universe?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-01T13:59:12-08:00","id":388884,"title":"","content":"Are you the same person you were yesterday at this same time, before having made whatever choices you did in the process? How about a year ago? Ten years?<br /> <br /> Are you the same person you will be tomorrow? Even if there are many, mutually contradictory tomorrow-people to be one with?<br /> <br /> Are their choices your choices, even if you haven't made them yet? And if not, how do they impact the meaning of your choices any more than the choices of other people with whom you don't share a temporal arc?<br /> <br /> Here's another question: what makes this question pressing to you? Is Owlman threatening to destroy our Earth? That guy's a dick.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-01T16:36:32-08:00","id":389104,"title":"","content":"He was evil Batman. Just like 'regular' Batman constantly struggles and fights an eternal war, Owlman quickly gave into that greatest of sins, despair.<br /> <br /> But even aside from that, most people don't base their every action on what is meaningful to the world beyond themselves. And living your life in response to how others live theirs, even if they are alternate versions of yourself, isn't a way to live.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-01T17:55:28-08:00","id":389166,"title":"","content":"Irrelevant for the most part. <br /> <br /> If there's a million other variations of the world out there, there is little point or value in it unless there was a way to exchange mass or information across them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-01T18:11:08-08:00","id":389189,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/388811-the-existence-of-the-multiverse-and-the-meaning-of-choice?p=388844#post388844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why did you post this when someone else might have in another universe?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hum....you actually raise a very good point. I'll take it into account for my next posts. :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-01T20:34:04-08:00","id":389369,"title":"","content":"These ideas come from the many-worlds interpretation of quantum physics, I imagine. Aren't the kind of &quot;events&quot; they talk about there meant to mean ideal quantum events, that is, the collapse or non-collapse (depending on which universe you are in) of a single wave function? So it's not actually like someone making a post on a forum or not, it's about stuff like a certain atom of radioactive material decaying or not at a certain point. Maybe I'm wrong (tell me if I am), but in that light, I feel like it's not a comparison I have to worry about.<br /> <br /> Even if we were talking about the bigger kinds of events, I still don't have much issue with the scenario laid out in the first post. We don't seem to be able to communicate past universe borders, so if someone made a post on a forum in another universe, that doesn't in any way affect mine. If I feel like a post on a forum is appropriate in this universe, then I will post one, and it will in no way be in vain just because someone might have done it in another universe.<br /> <br /> In fact, many people do the same things over and over again in this universe alone, and that doesn't make them irrelevant. Don't worry about originality, it's overrated. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-02T08:13:01-08:00","id":389860,"title":"","content":"It is kind of the same thing as the question &quot;What if time isn't linear...&quot;, &quot;If god already knows what you are going to do...&quot;, or any other question about choice. If you believe in free will then the answer is your choice isn't meaningless. If there is free will it doesn't matter if your choice has happened, is known, or someone in another universe is going to make a different choice. It was your choice to make and you will, did, or could make it. Ultimately your question boils down to, like with the others, is there free will or not?<br /> <br /> As to spefifically your question I would have to wonder if every choice we make has to have a different universe for it. The question I would have to ask is why? Even going for only the really important choices in a persons life, I would have to ask why a different universe? That seems excessively &quot;Humans are the center of the Universe&quot;. Maybe it is that way. I would think that at least it would be on a more global scale. Though even that seems like a small difference. Personally I would think it would be on a universal scale. Cosmic events that would shape difference universes. There might still be billions or more of you out there.<br /> <br /> And if that is the case then your choice matters even more because you are making it here in this Universe. Even if in another Universe someyou makes a similar choice when he wakes up tomorrow to walk his dogapus while the sun rises in the west, in that way, it was a different choice.<br /> <br /> Side thought: I'm sure like some others I've always wondered if maybe our creativity isn't creative, but mayhaps a glimpse into these other Universes?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forever and always forward.<br /> Don't ask why that came to mind or that I felt the need to post it.<br /> I see the incorporeally challenged.","edited":{"userid":787,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/787-sorwen","user":"Sorwen","date":". 02-02-2015, 12:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/787-sorwen","name":"Sorwen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-02T18:02:01-08:00","id":390727,"title":"","content":"Not to ruin your fun or anything, but a better question is &quot;Why does time only flow in one direction?&quot; Also the probability basis that is based on is a bit weird. It assumes that there's an infinite likelihood that something will occur, but we have a terrible understanding of how time works. We still have no real reason why time flows in one direction.<br /> <br /> Hell take the photon. According to relativity the photon exists at all points at once and all time points at once, or to say: the universe is a single point to a photon. Why? The math is correct, sure. No one knows why the universe is set up like that and anyone who says they do is a fool. Our universe is so impossibly complex that anyone saying they fully understand quantum mechanics is on the summit of Mount Stupid. <br /> <br /> The universe is weird and the best thing to do is assume it's simple and move on with your lives.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1VN49Y7tH2ZV0l7Hx65RWX1ez-Q9Lst-8ZTyTJeCTpxM/\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerer 20th</a> homebrew and my update to <a href=\"http://immortalthegathering.blogspot.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Highlander: the Gathering</a> for 20th Anniversary edition.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2414-theoutlander523","name":"theoutlander523","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-04T15:23:06-08:00","id":393131,"title":"","content":"Being decisive...making a choice is never meaningless...to you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-05T15:02:33-08:00","id":394153,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firanai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/388811-the-existence-of-the-multiverse-and-the-meaning-of-choice#post388811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#141823\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">There is a pressing question that I have had for some time. Imagine for one moment that there are an infinite number of realities out there, a multiverse, each one created by the different choices we have made and the ones we haven't. My question is, does the existence of other realities formed by our alternative choices make the very act of choice meaningless? I mean, what is the point of making any choice if out there in the infinity there is a universe in which we made the opposite choice? What meaning has any of our choices with infinite universe? I'm curious to know your opinions. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>You might be shocked, but I struggle with stuff like this all the time. Hell, even if you don't take into account a multi-verse, what meaning do our actions have compared to the vastness on the universe?<br /> <br /> So yea, I struggle with these ideas alot...<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorwen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/388811-the-existence-of-the-multiverse-and-the-meaning-of-choice?p=389860#post389860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As to spefifically your question I would have to wonder if every choice we make has to have a different universe for it. The question I would have to ask is why? Even going for only the really important choices in a persons life, I would have to ask why a different universe? That seems excessively &quot;Humans are the center of the Universe&quot;. Maybe it is that way. I would think that at least it would be on a more global scale. Though even that seems like a small difference. Personally I would think it would be on a universal scale. Cosmic events that would shape difference universes. There might still be billions or more of you out there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Heres the thing though, a multi-verse isn't based just on human actions. Theres potentially an infinite number universe, all based on the actions(or reactions) of everything. A rock tumbling down a hill goes slightly right than left. A dog runs out into the road. A bird trying to dodge a predator. An asteroid tumbling through space....on and on to infinity. It's crazy to think about or imagine, especially when take into account everything interacts, not just on this planet, but all planets, and all space in the universe.<br /> <br /> Thats of course assuming there is an infinite multi-verse.... There is some &quot;evidence&quot; for parallel universes I believe, but who knows exactly what that means...<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorwen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/388811-the-existence-of-the-multiverse-and-the-meaning-of-choice?p=389860#post389860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Side thought: I'm sure like some others I've always wondered if maybe our creativity isn't creative, but mayhaps a glimpse into these other Universes?</div> </div> </div> </div>What if dreams are?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>theoutlander523</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/388811-the-existence-of-the-multiverse-and-the-meaning-of-choice?p=390727#post390727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not to ruin your fun or anything, but a better question is &quot;Why does time only flow in one direction?&quot; Also the probability basis that is based on is a bit weird. It assumes that there's an infinite likelihood that something will occur, but we have a terrible understanding of how time works. We still have no real reason why time flows in one direction.</div> </div> </div> </div>Technically there is no time. But I know what you're saying. The crazy thing is, time can be manipulated by gravity and speed, slowed down, or sped up. But as for why we can only seem to go in one direction, that we don't know or understand yet..<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>theoutlander523</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/388811-the-existence-of-the-multiverse-and-the-meaning-of-choice?p=390727#post390727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hell take the photon. According to relativity the photon exists at all points at once and all time points at once, or to say: the universe is a single point to a photon. Why? The math is correct, sure. No one knows why the universe is set up like that and anyone who says they do is a fool. Our universe is so impossibly complex that anyone saying they fully understand quantum mechanics is on the summit of Mount Stupid.<br /> <br /> The universe is weird and the best thing to do is assume it's simple and move on with your lives.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty much. The universe is a strange place...<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/388811-the-existence-of-the-multiverse-and-the-meaning-of-choice?p=393131#post393131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Being decisive...making a choice is never meaningless...to you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly! In the &quot;grande scheme of things&quot; you and your actions might be meaningless. But right now, at this moment to you and those around you, actions are never meaningless.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-06T06:04:32-08:00","id":394715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firanai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/388811-the-existence-of-the-multiverse-and-the-meaning-of-choice#post388811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is a pressing question that I have had for some time. Imagine for one moment that there are an infinite number of realities out there, a multiverse, each one created by the different choices we have made and the ones we haven't. My question is, does the existence of other realities formed by our alternative choices make the very act of choice meaningless? I mean, what is the point of making any choice if out there in the infinity there is a universe in which we made the opposite choice? What meaning has any of our choices with infinite universe?</div> </div> </div> </div>If you truly think our choices are meaningless, then go jump in front of a bus. That choice won't matter, right? After all, some other version of you will have realized that would be an incredibly dumb thing to do and decided not to listen to me. Of course, at the same time, another version of you did decide to listen to me and immediately ran outside and jumped in front of a bus. I deeply apologize for getting that alternate-world version of you killed. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> But seriously, just because another hypothetical version of yourself makes a different choice from you (maybe a better one, maybe a worse one) in no way diminishes the choice that you have chosen to make, because you're living your own life, not theirs. I mean, hopefully though you'll make better choices than bizarro-you who decided to jump in front of that bus, or that other bizarro-you who decided to drink that whole gallon of Draino on a dare - at the least you should be glad that you're you and not those guys. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 02-06-2015, 01:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-06T13:58:03-08:00","id":395338,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr Gone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/388811-the-existence-of-the-multiverse-and-the-meaning-of-choice?p=394153#post394153\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What if dreams are?</div> </div> </div> </div>Then I feel really really really sorry for some other mes and the others can kiss my ass the lucky bastards.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forever and always forward.<br /> Don't ask why that came to mind or that I felt the need to post it.<br /> I see the incorporeally challenged.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/787-sorwen","name":"Sorwen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-06T17:57:09-08:00","id":395680,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/388811-the-existence-of-the-multiverse-and-the-meaning-of-choice?p=394715#post394715\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you truly think our choices are meaningless, then go jump in front of a bus. That choice won't matter, right? After all, some other version of you will have realized that would be an incredibly dumb thing to do and decided not to listen to me. Of course, at the same time, another version of you did decide to listen to me and immediately ran outside and jumped in front of a bus. I deeply apologize for getting that alternate-world version of you killed. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> But seriously, just because another hypothetical version of yourself makes a different choice from you (maybe a better one, maybe a worse one) in no way diminishes the choice that you have chosen to make, because you're living your own life, not theirs. I mean, hopefully though you'll make better choices than bizarro-you who decided to jump in front of that bus, or that other bizarro-you who decided to drink that whole gallon of Draino on a dare - at the least you should be glad that you're you and not those guys. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Nah don't worry about it, I'm reasonable sure that I wouldn't get along with my other selves. I'm the cool one :P. I was just curious about your opinions on the matter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-07T14:52:57-08:00","id":396801,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr Gone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/388811-the-existence-of-the-multiverse-and-the-meaning-of-choice?p=394153#post394153\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What if dreams are?</div> </div> </div> </div>Then I want to go visit that universe that did an actual credits roll at the end of the dream I had, because that was cool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-07T16:25:49-08:00","id":396898,"title":"","content":"<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><b>Misaka #10032:</b> &quot;What are you doing?&quot; asks Misaka. I cannot understand your actions. As long as the necessary equipment and chemicals are available, Misaka can be automatically manufactured at the touch of a button. Fabricated bodies stocked with borrowed minds, at a unit price of \u00a5180,000. There are still 9968 unused units in stock. For the sake of someone like that, you\u2014<br /> <br /> <b>Toma:</b> It doesn't matter. Fabricated bodies, or borrowed minds\u2014 little things like that don't make any difference. I'm standing here to rescue you, since there's only one of you in the whole world.<br /> <br /> <i>A Certain Scientific Railgun</i></div>A scene dealing with one of 20,000 clones questioning her value, rather than alternate realities; but the underlying point is still applicable. There may be an infinite number of alternate versions of you out there who have made different choices in the past; but there\u2019s only one of you here and now, facing the choice you\u2019re about to make \u2014 and whichever way you choose, you\u2019re going to have to deal with the consequences of that choice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-07T17:10:49-08:00","id":396960,"title":"","content":"I am curious, would any of you get along with your alternative selves? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-07T19:02:21-08:00","id":397065,"title":"","content":"One day, somebody is going to write a fiction containing something that approximates closer to what actual multiverse theories are like; where something as abstract and complex and emergent as the human perception of &quot;choice&quot; is not the differentiating factor, but observations of quantum phenomena are. In short, the alternate universes don't contain the consequences of choices you never made (which is already something that would have to be so complex and enormous that it would already be beyond comprehension; these fictions always assume that it's <i>your</i> choice that matters, or ones where vast numbers of choices are all vaguely unified by some abstract quality, hardly anybody ever considers that there would have to be a universe for each potential decision that, say, an early proto-human made), but one where, well, almost everything is the same, it's just that certain observational data of elementary particles was different. The other universe me is doing the exact same things at the exact same time for the exact same reasons, he's just oriented against the particles composing electricity in the computer screen at a different angle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov