value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-09T12:14:08-08:00","id":399161,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firanai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/388811-the-existence-of-the-multiverse-and-the-meaning-of-choice?p=396960#post396960\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am curious, would any of you get along with your alternative selves? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><img src=\"http://i3.kym-cdn.com/photos/images/newsfeed/000/694/181/fe4.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Well, probably not <i>that</i> well, but I imagine I'd get along with my alternate self, as long as he wasn't a serial killer or anything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-09T16:48:42-08:00","id":399533,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/388811-the-existence-of-the-multiverse-and-the-meaning-of-choice?p=399161#post399161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><img src=\"http://i3.kym-cdn.com/photos/images/newsfeed/000/694/181/fe4.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Well, probably not <i>that</i> well, but I imagine I'd get along with my alternate self, as long as he wasn't a serial killer or anything.</div> </div> </div> </div>That image is incredibly disturbing and hilarious at the same time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-14T06:48:11-08:00","id":405751,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firanai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/388811-the-existence-of-the-multiverse-and-the-meaning-of-choice#post388811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#141823\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">There is a pressing question that I have had for some time. Imagine for one moment that there are an infinite number of realities out there, a multiverse, each one created by the different choices we have made and the ones we haven't. My question is, does the existence of other realities formed by our alternative choices make the very act of choice meaningless? I mean, what is the point of making any choice if out there in the infinity there is a universe in which we made the opposite choice? What meaning has any of our choices with infinite universe? I'm curious to know your opinions. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=1tag9Pm3qtA\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=1tag9Pm3qtA</a></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The meaning of choice is whatever you decide or don't decide it to be, in both its absolutes and its relatives. After all, anything that is meaningless has meaning and anything that has meaning is meaningless. The very idea that the answer to your question poses a choice for the person choosing the answer is in itself both meaningful and meaningless to both the inquirer of the question of choice and the responder who chooses what the answer is. Even when it comes to choice, whether or not you have a choice or don't have a choice exists coincidentally, therefore, my answer to your question based on my choice and my lack of choice, both simultaneously and separately is simply this:<br /> <br /> The ten thousand things and nothing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>How can I know if what I claim I know to be true is rejecting the idea that there is something I might not know? How can I know if what I claim I don't know to be true is rejecting the idea that there is something I do know?<br /> -Zhuangzi","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1715-ostarion","name":"Ostarion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1715_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"305"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-15T07:28:38-08:00","id":406684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/388811-the-existence-of-the-multiverse-and-the-meaning-of-choice?p=397065#post397065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The other universe me is doing the exact same things at the exact same time for the exact same reasons, he's just oriented against the particles composing electricity in the computer screen at a different angle.</div> </div> </div> </div>Very true, in fact, as can be read in Robert Omnes &quot;The Interpretation of Quantum Mechanics&quot; really those two versions of &quot;you&quot; are one version. The universe split really only occurs on the atomic level, there is still one classical/macroscopic world, i.e. the atoms in the screen have two histories, you do not. A major part of the modern Everett interpretation is that parsing what happens to an atom in situations like this as &quot;multiple worlds&quot; is attempting to use the classical concept of a consistent history on objects that don't possess one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3326-an-fhuiseog","name":"An Fhuiseog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3326_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[